   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "The Korean won weakened against the U.S. dollar Friday, as global oil prices surged over renewed uncertainties about the war in the Middle East. The won was quoted at 1,336.7 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., down 6 won from the close of the previous stock trading session.",
   "summary_zh": "受中东战事不确定性再度升温、全球油价飙升影响，韩元周五兑美元走弱。下午3时30分，韩元兑美元报1,336.7韩元，较上一股市交易日收盘时下跌6韩元。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Korean won weakened against the U.S. dollar Friday, as global oil prices surged over renewed uncertainties about the war in the Middle East. The won was quoted at 1,336.7 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., down 6 won from the close of the previous stock trading session. Brent crude futures jumped 3.3 percent at $95.82 per barrel after U.S. President Donald Trump said there is no need for a deal with Iran. Iran's media also reported that oil tankers were hit by explosions in the Strait of Hormuz. Foreign investors sold a net 550 billion won ($411 million) worth of local shares during the latest regular stock trading session, while the benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index fell 0.98 percent to close at 5,290.53",
