   "title": "Former Wescom chief Alan Javier takes helm of Philippine Navy",
   "url": "https://www.inquirer.net/495567/former-wescom-chief-alan-javier-takes-helm-of-philippine-navy/",
   "domain": "inquirer.net",
   "source": "inquirer.net",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:46:14 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794581174.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Before his appointment, Javier headed Wescom, which oversees military operations in Palawan and the West Philippine Sea, where Chinese vessels have repeatedly challenged Philippine maritime activities. “Vice Admiral Javier brings with him the operational urgency and strategic direction needed to lead the Philippine Navy and sustain our naval operations,” Defense spokesperson Arsenio Andolong said in a statement.",
   "summary_zh": "在上任之前，哈维尔曾负责西部司令部，该司令部负责监督菲律宾在巴拉望岛和西菲律宾海的军事行动；中国船只曾多次对菲律宾的海上活动提出挑战。国防部发言人阿塞尼奥·安多隆在一份声明中说：“哈维尔中将带来了领导菲律宾海军、维持海军行动所需的紧迫感和战略方向。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. presided over the change of command and retirement ceremony at the Philippine Navy headquarters in Manila on Nov. 13. Before his appointment, Javier headed Wescom, which oversees military operations in Palawan and the West Philippine Sea, where Chinese vessels have repeatedly challenged Philippine maritime activities. He also previously served as commander of the Western Naval Command, formerly known as Naval Forces West, and as chief of Naval Staff. The Department of National Defense (DND) welcomed Javier’s appointment, citing his experience in naval operations and military leadership. “Vice Admiral Javier brings with him the operational urgency and strategic direction needed to lead the Philippine Navy and sustain our naval operations,” Defense spokesperson Arsenio Andolong said in a statement. Javier takes over the Navy as the Philippines continues to modernize its maritime forces and strengthen its presence in the West Philippine Sea amid persistent tensions with China. Beijing claims nearly the entire South China Sea, including waters within the Philippines’ exclusive economic zone, despite a 2016 arbitral ruling that invalidated its sweeping maritime claims. The DND also thanked Ezpeleta for his more than 35 years of military service as he retired from the Armed Forces of the Philippines. /mr",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ph",
    "vn"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
