   "title": "Andhra Pradesh emerges as a leader in India’s rooftop solar push: Union Minister",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/andhra-pradesh-emerges-as-a-leader-in-indias-rooftop-solar-push-union-minister/article71697838.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:14:18 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794581058.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Union Minister for New and Renewable Energy Pralhad Joshi has said that India has made remarkable progress in ensuring energy security, with Andhra Pradesh playing a significant role through rooftop solar installations and solar-powered agricultural pump sets. India’s solar power capacity had expanded from 2.80 GW in 2014 to 175 GW, he said, adding that non-fossil sources now accounted for nearly 55% of the country’s total installed power generation capacity.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。印度新任可再生能源部长Pralhad Joshi表示，印度在确保能源安全方面取得了显著进展，其中安得拉邦通过屋顶太阳能设施和太阳能农用泵组发挥了重要作用。他说，印度的太阳能发电装机容量已从2014年的2.80 GW扩大到175 GW，非化石能源目前占该国总发电装机容量的近55%。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Union Minister for New and Renewable Energy Pralhad Joshi has said that India has made remarkable progress in ensuring energy security, with Andhra Pradesh playing a significant role through rooftop solar installations and solar-powered agricultural pump sets. Addressing a session on ‘Securing the Sustainable Future: Energy Resilience, Clean Technologies and Global Partnership’ at the 31st CII Partnership Summit 2026, he said the country’s peak power demand had risen from 123 GW in 2012 to 270 GW. Recalling the grid collapse in 2012 that plunged north India into darkness for nearly 72 hours, he said the country was now meeting the increased demand without interruption, with nearly 33% of the power sourced from non-fossil fuels. India’s solar power capacity had expanded from 2.80 GW in 2014 to 175 GW, he said, adding that non-fossil sources now accounted for nearly 55% of the country’s total installed power generation capacity. India was on course to achieve its target of 500 GW of non-fossil fuel capacity by 2030. Mr. Joshi said Andhra Pradesh had enabled 7.86 lakh households to install rooftop solar systems. Under the PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana, 66 lakh households across the country had benefited against the target of one crore. Reiterating Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s vision of ‘Zero Defect, Zero Effect’ manufacturing, he said green energy would help India emerge as a global hub for green manufacturing. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "ene",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_thehindu",
   "title_zh": "印度联邦部长：安得拉邦成为印度屋顶太阳能推广的领跑者",
   "body_zh": "订阅可享受会员专享报道、社论、观点等更多权益。与《The Hindu》一同订阅，即可解锁这些内容。新任可再生能源和新能源部长Pralhad Joshi表示，印度在保障能源安全方面取得了显著进展，其中安得拉邦通过屋顶太阳能装置和太阳能农用泵组发挥了重要作用。他在第31届CII伙伴关系峰会2026年会议“保障可持续未来：能源韧性、清洁技术与全球伙伴关系”分会致辞时表示，该国最高电力需求已从2012年的123 GW增至270 GW。他回顾了2012年导致印度北部陷入近72小时黑暗的电网崩溃事件，并表示，如今该国能够不间断地满足增加后的需求，其中近33%的电力来自非化石燃料。他说，印度的太阳能发电装机容量已从2014年的2.80 GW扩大到175 GW，非化石能源目前占该国总装机发电能力的近55%。印度正稳步实现到2030年将非化石燃料装机容量提升至500 GW的目标。Joshi先生表示，安得拉邦已帮助78.6万户家庭安装屋顶太阳能系统。在PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana计划下，全国已有660万户家庭受益，而目标是为1000万户家庭提供支持。他再次强调总理Narendra Modi关于“零缺陷、零影响”制造的愿景，并表示，绿色能源将帮助印度成为全球绿色制造中心。评论须以英文完整句撰写，不得含有辱骂性或人身攻击性内容。请遵守我们的社区评论准则。我们已迁移至新的评论平台。如果您已是《The Hindu》的注册用户并已登录，可以继续参与文章互动。如果您尚无账户，请注册并登录后发表评论。用户登录账户后可在Vuukle查看以往发表的评论",
