   "_dt": 1794580999.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription ABB India on Friday reported a 10% year-on-year (YoY) increase in net profit to ₹440 crore for the third quarter of CY2026, while revenue grew 19% to ₹3,738 crore. The company’s order inflows surged 56% YoY to ₹4,733 crore, marking a quarterly record. Its order backlog stood at ₹12,927 crore, up 36% from the year-ago period.",
   "summary_zh": "解锁这些内容需订阅。ABB India于周五报告称，2026自然年第三季度净利润同比增长10%，达到440亿卢比，营收增长19%，达到3,738亿卢比。公司新增订单额同比增长56%，达到4,733亿卢比，创下季度纪录。期末未完成订单额为12,927亿卢比，较去年同期增长36%。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription ABB India on Friday reported a 10% year-on-year (YoY) increase in net profit to ₹440 crore for the third quarter of CY2026, while revenue grew 19% to ₹3,738 crore. The company’s order inflows surged 56% YoY to ₹4,733 crore, marking a quarterly record. Its order backlog stood at ₹12,927 crore, up 36% from the year-ago period. Electrification led order growth, with gains across all segments. The Motion business witnessed growth in select segments, particularly railways and services, while Automation, despite remaining muted, recorded an increase in export orders. Key growth drivers included data centres, utilities, metals and mining, food and beverages, cement, buildings and infrastructure, the company said. Despite a dynamic operating environment, the company remained focused on disciplined execution and operational performance, he said. “Looking ahead, India’s structural growth drivers in industrialisation, electrification, digitalisation and the energy transition continue to support attractive growth opportunities, positioning us well for the quarters ahead,” Mr. Sharma added. Demand was further supported by investments in data centres, grid modernisation, renewable energy integration and energy-transition projects, alongside capital expenditure across metals, cement, railways and buildings. business (general) / earnings / company information / manufacturing and engineering Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
