   "title": "Vision Digital India, A.P. govt. sign MoU to set up AI training centres",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/vision-digital-india-ap-govt-sign-mou-to-set-up-ai-training-centres/article71696976.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:01:35 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794580295.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Vision Digital India Chairman Harikrishna Maram presents a portrait to Minister for IT and Education Nara Lokesh at the CII Partnership Summit in Visakhapatnam on Friday. Vision Digital India, Bengaluru, will set up artificial intelligence (AI) training centres in selected educational institutions in association with the Andhra Pradesh government.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅可解锁这些内容：Vision Digital India董事长Harikrishna Maram于周五在维沙卡帕特南举行的CII伙伴关系峰会上向IT与教育部长Nara Lokesh赠送一幅肖像。总部位于班加罗尔的Vision Digital India将联合安得拉邦政府，在部分教育机构设立人工智能（AI）培训中心。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Vision Digital India Chairman Harikrishna Maram presents a portrait to Minister for IT and Education Nara Lokesh at the CII Partnership Summit in Visakhapatnam on Friday. Vision Digital India, Bengaluru, will set up artificial intelligence (AI) training centres in selected educational institutions in association with the Andhra Pradesh government. Company chairman Harikrishna Maram signed a memorandum of understanding (MoU) with the State government in the presence of Chief Minister N. Chandrababu Naidu and Minister for IT and Education Nara Lokesh at the CII Partnership Summit in Visakhapatnam. He exchanged the MoU documents with Mr. Lokesh. In a press release on Friday, Mr. Harikrishna said the initiative would provide practical AI training to thousands of youngsters in Vizianagaram, Visakhapatnam and other parts of the State. He said human intelligence would remain more powerful than artificial intelligence and that AI would not take away jobs, despite the initial challenges posed by technological advancements. He added that his company had already signed MoUs with several educational institutions in Vizianagaram and expressed hope that the proposed training facilities would benefit students from marginalised sections as well. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
