   "title": "Kwara PDP Guber Candidate Unveils Agenda, Promises N100b Security Trust Fund",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/kwara-pdp-guber-candidate-unveils-agenda-promises-n100b-security-trust-fund/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:16:14 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794579374.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "Kawu made the pledge during the public presentation of his manifesto, titled, THE SBK COMPACT – KWARA PEOPLE FIRST (KPF) in Ilorin, the state capital. He said that the security Trust Fund would provide fund for intelligence-led operations, stronger community partnerships, well-equipped and coordinated security services and a government-wide system that identifies threats, responds quickly and holds agencies accountable for risks.",
   "summary_zh": "卡武在伊洛林——该州首府——公开介绍其题为《THE SBK COMPACT – KWARA PEOPLE FIRST (KPF)》的竞选宣言时作出上述承诺。他说，安全信托基金将提供资金，用于开展以情报为引领的行动、加强社区伙伴关系、装备充足且协同配合的安全服务，以及建立一套覆盖整个政府的体系，以识别威胁、迅速作出响应，并督促各机构为风险承担责任。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Kawu made the pledge during the public presentation of his manifesto, titled, THE SBK COMPACT – KWARA PEOPLE FIRST (KPF) in Ilorin, the state capital. He said that the security Trust Fund would provide fund for intelligence-led operations, stronger community partnerships, well-equipped and coordinated security services and a government-wide system that identifies threats, responds quickly and holds agencies accountable for risks. “Security is the foundation of development. The first responsibility of government is to protect the lives, property and livelihoods of the governed. This aspect of the contract is for the people who have lost somebody dear to them. It is for our people who have been displaced from their homes as a result of banditry and kidnapping. It is for those who have been prevented from freely conducting their businesses. To restore the glory of our State as the State of Harmony, we will establish a 100 billion naira security trust fund to tackle insecurity,” he said. Kawu also announced plan by his administration to establish a N40bn One Kwara Regional Development Agency if elected to deliver on viable projects and to ensure equitable development across all the communities in the state. He also said that a minimum of N5bn would be provided as counterpart funding for donor funding sources in this area over four years. “In addition, our government will introduce a special grassroots development initiative under which N50 million will be allocated to each of the 193 wards in the state within the first 100 days of our administration. This represents a total initial commitment of ₦9.65 billion. Under this initiative, development projects will originate directly from the various wards. “Communities will identify and choose their most pressing needs, propose projects and participate in their implementation. Required mechanisms will be put in place to ensure transparency, accountability, technical supervision and value for money,” he added. Kawu also said that his government would introduce a 13th month salary for every civil servant in the state. He added that his government would create 200,000 new youth employment opportunities and 5,000 enterprise opportunities annually. “We will support women-owned businesses by establishing a ₦3 billion Women Enterprises and Empowerment Fund to provide affordable finance and business support to our women-owned enterprises. “Also, artisans and skilled workers will enjoy business support grants. At least 1,000 artisans will benefit from this grant annually”, Kawu said. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
