   "title": "Korea's rice production falls for 5th year in 2026 amid changing diets",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/20261113/koreas-rice-production-falls-for-5th-year-in-2026-amid-changing-diets",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:52:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794559923.0,
   "ageDays": 0.26,
   "summary": "Korea's rice output declined for the fifth consecutive year in 2026 amid changing dietary habits, data showed Friday, with the cultivation area also reaching a new low. Rice production decreased 0.9 percent year-on-year to 3.5 million tons this year, according to data compiled by the Ministry of Data and Statistics. Rice remains a staple food in Korea, but consumption has steadily fallen in recent decades amid shifts in dietary preferences.",
   "summary_zh": "数据显示，受饮食习惯变化影响，韩国稻米产量在2026年连续第5年下降，种植面积也降至历史新低。数据统计部汇总的数据显示，今年韩国稻米产量同比下降0.9%，降至350万吨。稻米仍是韩国的主食，但随着饮食偏好的变化，近几十年来消费量持续下降。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea's rice output declined for the fifth consecutive year in 2026 amid changing dietary habits, data showed Friday, with the cultivation area also reaching a new low. Rice production decreased 0.9 percent year-on-year to 3.5 million tons this year, according to data compiled by the Ministry of Data and Statistics. It marked the fourth-lowest level since the government began compiling the data in 1965. The combined area of rice paddies in the country fell 1.1 percent year-on-year to 670,000 hectares, the smallest on record. Despite the decline in overall production, output per 1,000 square meters increased 0.2 percent year-on-year to 524 kilograms this year, according to the ministry. Rice remains a staple food in Korea, but consumption has steadily fallen in recent decades amid shifts in dietary preferences. The decrease in production also came amid the government's efforts to manage output while encouraging farmers to switch to other crops. By region, South Jeolla Province and Gwangju together produced 736,000 tons of rice, followed by South Chungcheong Province with 681,000 tons and North Jeolla Province with 526,000 tons, the government findings showed",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
